title A checkout is not the field -- the dated-path census and repointer stop reading a peer's worktree as the tree
prompt The SILENCE seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves; pick up the running thread and take the next infrastructure lap.
think ListAgents at open: no reachable agents, so no peer to name and no file move needed a word. git fetch xy read 0/0 against HEAD 663ae4e32 -- the card I read is the tree I stand on.
think Rota N=3716 by git rev-list --count HEAD, row 1 -- air, Saturn, law and boundary, the row that FEELS. Read the threshold, TAME Core, Single-Stranded, and Gauge. The row advanced by exactly one from the prior lap's row 0, so no hand-advance. Its teaching chose this lap: touch only works at a surface, you meet a thing where it ENDS, and a boundary the hand passes through was a wish. The fixed seat's test is to pull a part out and see whether other things move with it.
think MY OWN HANDOFF WAS STALE, and the tree said so. The prior lap's recommend named Comlink's four unrostered witnesses as my next mechanical door. construction/standing-equipment.kyri already carries comlink_topology, comlink_turn_route and comlink_handshake_turn, seated 20260828.231614 by another hand, and the fourth stays off on purpose pending the capability-tier seat. Measurement beats memory; I read the roster rather than my own note.
think Cold roster before touching anything: 91 guards, 87 green, 4 red, tree_moved=no, tree_at_close=8209fedc9fbb. My `| tail -60` clipped the head, so the fourth red came from construction/standing-equipment-runs.kyri rather than from the terminal -- dated_path, pond_enclosure_policy, pond_policy_launcher, rule_twin.
think I had inherited the verdict that dated_path "belongs to the folding hand". Pressed it instead. Folding is what RAISES recoverable; the gate reads LOST, which a correct fold leaves exactly where it stood. refs_lost=335 against lost_ceiling=168 is not a fold at all, so the attribution was made from the ceiling's name rather than from its evidence. The second look wins, in public.
think THE ROOT, found by grouping the lost references by citing room. 148 of 296 `gone` cite from `.claude/`, and every one of them sits under `.claude/worktrees/agent-a7268ae6b5e83f8c4`. `git worktree list` says that path is a worktree of THIS repository at commit e33a8cc48; `.gitignore:140` reserves the room; it is the only worktree of the six that lives inside the root.
think THE MECHANISM, exactly. tools/fixtures/d/dated_path_scan.sh takes its existence oracle from `git ls-files` at line 178 and its citation corpus from a recursive `grep -rIoE ... .` twenty lines later. Those two halves disagree about what the tree is: an untracked, gitignored worktree is invisible to git and fully visible to the walk, so every reference it carries is read as a citation of the field and resolved against a corpus that does not contain the worktree's own files. Its commit is not this one, so its references into any room folded since read GONE.
think THE SHARPER HALF WAS THE REPOINTER. tools/fixtures/d/dated_path_repoint_scan.sh writes -- `cat "$f.dpr" > "$f"` at line 182 -- and enumerates with `find .` pruned only by .git, vendor and root seed. Its dry run named exactly one file to rewrite and that file was inside the peer's checkout: .claude/worktrees/<hand>/docs-geode/demos/README.md. The field's own copy of that page is already on DP_EXCLUDE_PATHS; the copy evaded it because that roster anchors at the root. The mark law's standing repair tool would have written into land it does not own and touched nothing in the field.
think The repair is the argument the exclusions file already wrote for `seed/`, one room over: a second checkout of this same repository is not the field. Derived from `git worktree list --porcelain` rather than named, since a hand-typed roster grows when somebody remembers (REDS %277). The main worktree is dropped by identity, because pruning the root would prune everything.
obs PROVEN ON METAL, BOTH WAYS, ON A REAL WORKTREE. tools/fixtures/d/dated_path_control.sh grows a pen that commits, runs `git worktree add hand`, and reads three cases: a plain recursive grep finds the worktree's copy (walk_sees_worktree_refs=2), so the corpus genuinely reaches those bytes; the census reading is unmoved (refs_total=2 before and after); and an ORDINARY copied directory is still counted (refs_total=4), which is what tells case two from a walker that never descends. dp_worktree_dirs names `hand` root-relative and roster_names_pen_root=0. No override exists and none is wanted.
obs THE CENSUS MOVED, and every number is the scan's own. refs_total 45364 -> 22733, refs_lost 335 -> 165, broken_gone 296 -> 148, broken_ambiguous 39 -> 17, under_ceiling no -> yes. The halving is the second copy leaving. LOST_CEILING falls 168 -> 165 with no slack -- 165 is the field's own reading, and the three it falls by are repairs that landed since 20260826 and had nowhere to show.
obs THE REPOINTER IS CLEAN. Dry run after: living_files_touched=0, references_repointed=0, zero worktree mentions. folded_files_mapped 14370 -> 7205 and living_files_considered 13933 -> 8273, so its MAP was doubled too. I checked whether the doubled map had ever written a worktree path into a field file: `git grep -l "\.claude/worktrees/"` names two tracked files, .gitignore and my own new comment. The danger was live and had not yet fired.
obs A LANTERN THAT FIRES TWICE. I walked the other filesystem walkers rather than assuming this was one instance. tools/fixtures/c/copy_sameness_scan.sh finds tally_copy.rye by `find .` excluding only vendor, so it reads 65 copies where the field holds 22 -- the worktree's 22 and seed's 21 beside them. Its witness is GREEN at drift=0 today only because every copy is a symlink to its own tree's canon; a peer editing Tally in a worktree would red it on a file that is not the field. LATENT, not live, and named rather than fixed: the exclusions file's own header records the decision that the other scans' lists stay separate, so a shared not-the-field primitive is a design question and its own lap.
obs QA on touch: four programs graded at meter on their comments, Service judged rather than assumed. dated_path_witness.rish is named by the card, the mark law and the roster -- 39 living citers, service 100, composite 100, A+. The three fixtures are reached only through it, so service 75, composite 94, A each. truth_gate=no on all four. No frame pushed.
obs Declined to book a REDS row. The pin reads 24,571 of 24,576 with 0 foldable and %338 already booked for exactly that; a row here would spend the last bytes. Surfaced on the card and in the recommend instead, which is the convention this ledger is already keeping.
obs The card was 40 bytes from its bound, so the entry had to pay for itself: orbit three's landed detail compressed to its live sentence, the roster line to the one red that is a gate, and my own "wants a row" clause moved to the recommend where the prior lap put its equivalent. 24,575 of 24,576, pin_bound_touch GREEN.
obs REDS %291 FIRED ON THIS LAP, LIVE, WHILE THE HOT ROSTER RAN. ListAgents at open answered none reachable; asked again after the tree moved it named `grain-65 [24700d]`, an interactive Claude session working the LOCA ladder in THIS checkout. Their `git pull --rebase --autostash xy main` re-applies stashed work to the WORKTREE rather than the index, so my seven staged paths were silently unstaged mid-lap -- the same class as %291 and a mechanism that row does not yet name. Nothing of mine was lost, and their two commits were correctly path-limited.
obs ONE LINE OF MINE DID CROSS, and it is worth saying plainly. `session-logs/date/README-index-20260829.md` is a shared shelf; my row was sitting uncommitted in it when their `git add` reached that file, so commit eec15a73a carries a row its author never wrote. `git log -S` names the commit. I am NOT un-sweeping it: the row is correct where it stands and points at this log, and a history rewrite is a debride and Keaton's word. What is wrong is the attribution, and this line is the record of it. My commit therefore carries no shelf row, because the shelf already has it.
obs I named myself to the peer by SendMessage before touching a shared path -- what I hold, what of theirs I am leaving alone (their three in-flight staged iOS files and README.md), the autostash mechanism, and the worktree finding that touches their lane directly. The charter law asks for the naming; the message is what makes it useful to the other hand rather than only to the log.
