scope infrastructure Glow -- the dated-path census and repointer, and the boundary between a tree and a checkout of it
status landed GREEN on metal; three roster reds remain, all gated or another bench's
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- %291 FIRED WHILE THIS LAP RAN: a peer (`grain-65`) is working the SAME checkout, its `pull --rebase --autostash` unstaged my seven paths mid-lap, and its `git add` on the shared day shelf carried one row of mine into commit eec15a73a. Nothing lost, no sweep of my tool changes, peer named by SendMessage before I touched a shared path -- and the autostash mechanism is one %291 does not yet name. A RED CLOSED AT ITS ROOT: dated_path read 335 lost against a ceiling of 168 because a peer's worktree inside `.claude/` is a second checkout of this repository and the census walked it. Both tools prune in-root worktrees now, derived from `git worktree list`, and the ceiling falls 168 -> 165 with the field's own reading. THE HALF WORTH YOUR EYE: the repointer WRITES, and its dry run named exactly one file to rewrite -- inside that peer's checkout, nothing in the field. Nothing had fired yet; two tracked files mention the path and both are honest. WANTS A ROW WHEN THE PIN CAN HOLD ONE (%338 is holding it): `copy_sameness_scan.sh` walks the same worktree and `seed/` -- 65 copies where the field holds 22 -- green today only because they are symlinks. A shared not-the-field primitive across scans is a design question the exclusions file deliberately left open, so it is named rather than guessed. STANDING, unchanged and yours: rule_twin 39/36 is gate %7, the REDS pin is full, and the two Pond reds are a macOS bench fact. MINE, MECHANICAL, IF YOU WANT IT NEXT: the capability tier for comlink_r1_dual_stack's IPv6 leg -- the roster comment already reasons it out, that `host` is a tier for PLACE and this one is CAPABILITY.
